                <pb facs="0718" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg630"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Barrett.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis informs Mr. Barrett that the Secretary of War will be the guests of
                    the Panama Canal Commission and of this Government, and that the fleet will
                    remain at Panama. Instructs him to inform the President of Panama.)</p>
            </div>
